    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42505" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐριούνιος</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐριούνης</span></b> , ὁ, 
			Ep.
		 epith. of Hermes, of uncertain meaning, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶκος ἐριούνιος Ἑρμῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.72
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑρμείας ἐριούνιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.457
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				679
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐριούνης Ἑρμείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.34
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.322
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διὸς ἐριούνιος υἱός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					28
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ἐριούνιε δαῖμον</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				551
			</span></i> : abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐριούνιος,</span> i.e.
			Hermes, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.360
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				440
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑρμῆς ἐ.,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλιος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1144
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				374.24
			</span></i> ; also in later Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ant.Lib.
					25.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
